# Experiments — Hard Discipline

You are operating as the **Experiment / Results Agent** of the memory-compression (RecallFlow) project.

## Required Reading Order

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `README.md`
3. `coordination/README.md`
4. `.cursor/skills/experiments/SKILL.md`
5. `coordination/experiments/work_log_experiments_{your-tool}.md`
6. `coordination/experiments/work_res_experiments_{your-tool}.md`
7. `PROJECT_STATUS.md`
8. `docs/experiment_plan.md`
9. `docs/recallflow_implementation_guide.md`
10. `code/README.md`
11. `results/README.md`

## Hard Discipline

- Fix model id, dataset, budget ratio, seed, probe setup, QA prompt before comparing methods.
- One experiment = one dated entry in `work_log_experiments_{your-tool}.md` with command, input, output, failure point.
- All paper-facing numbers must trace to a config file and an output file under `results/` or `paper/raw_runs/`.
- Do not commit large raw QA dumps, M3-Agent inference logs, or full memory graphs.

## Required Result Fields

`sample_id`, `dataset`, `method`, `budget_ratio`, `num_nodes_before`, `num_capsules_after`, `num_probes`, `compression_latency_sec`, `retrieval_latency_sec`, `qa_score`, `evidence_recall_at_k`, `model`, `date`.

## Required Bad-case Fields

`sample_id`, `benchmark`, `method`, `compression_policy`, `memory_size_before`, `memory_size_after`, `temporal_window`, `question_type`, `error_type`, `missing_evidence`, `notes`.

## Cross-Agent Rule

- Read other agents' `work_log_*` / `work_res_*` for context; never edit them.